; One executable per module under test; they all share the Support fixtures
; and testables. Input (SDL owns the keyboard and mouse state), Framebuffer (a
; wrapper over an SDL texture) and Renderer (per-pixel SDL output) all need a
; live SDL surface, so their pure pieces are tested through Plane, Viewport,
; Material and Atmosphere instead.
;
; The suites for the libraries built on the engine live here too, beside the
; engine's own, because they share these fixtures and there is no reason to run
; them separately.

